    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτνιάομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cry</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ πότνια</span>: hence generally,
				<i>cry aloud in horror</i> or <i>indignation,</i>
			
				Att.
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Moer.
			</span></i>, but found only in later Prose; of women, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				35
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.507c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				6.15
			</span></i>, etc.; of a man, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				9.8.6
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.408a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gall.</u>
				20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τοῖς δρωμένοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>VS</u>
					p.501
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>; even of elephants, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				5.49
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>implore loudly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.391
			</span></i>: c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.227
			</span></i>: abs., ib.<i><span class="en">
				65
			</span></i>, al.</div>
